    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d81">

                <pb facs="0149" n="57" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg57"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt
                    Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d81-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-10-31">31 October 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Prime Minister to President. Number 482. Most secret and personal.</p>
                <p>My immediately preceding telegram, para 1: Your humble servant, yourself and the
                        Generalissimo respectively.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d81-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d81-f1-content">
                <p>Apparently sent to Washington via military channels, and forwarded by the White
                    House Map Room to Roosevelt at Hyde
                    Park.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
